---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// Disclosure under § 25 MedienG: name and place of residence.
const owner = 'Thomas Hochörtler';
const residence = 'Kindberg, Austria';
// Contact for privacy requests (Art. 13 GDPR).
const contact = 'hochitom@me.com';
---
<Base title="Imprint & privacy" description="Who runs hochitom.rocks, which data the site processes and where the map data comes from.">
  <article class="imprint">
    <h1 class="page-title">Imprint &amp; privacy</h1>

    <section>
      <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
      <p>
        hochitom.rocks is my private catalogue of Hard Rock Cafe pins. It has no ads, sells nothing and is not
        connected to Hard Rock Cafe in any way.
      </p>
      <p>Disclosure under § 25 MedienG (Austrian Media Act):</p>
      <p class="disclosure">
        {owner}<br />
        {residence}
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        I am responsible for the processing of personal data on this site. You can reach me at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by Netlify. When you open a page, Netlify’s servers receive the usual request data, such
        as your IP address, the page you asked for, the time and your browser’s user agent, and keep it in server logs
        for a short time to deliver the site and keep it secure. Netlify processes this data on my behalf;
        see <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/">Netlify’s privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        To see how many people visit and which pins they look at, I use Cloudflare Web Analytics. Each page loads a
        small script from Cloudflare, so your browser sends Cloudflare your IP address, browser’s user agent, the
        page address, the referring page and page load times. Cloudflare uses this to give me visitor statistics
        and, according to its own statement, does not use it to track you across sites. The script sets no cookies
        and stores nothing on your device, which is why there is no cookie banner.
        See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Both are processed on the basis of my legitimate interest in running the site securely and knowing whether
        anyone looks at it (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Netlify and Cloudflare are US companies, so data may be transferred
        to the USA; both are certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework.
      </p>
      <p>
        The fonts are served from this site itself, so your browser makes no requests to Google or any other font
        service. There are no contact forms, comments or accounts, so I collect nothing else about you.
      </p>
      <p>
        You have the right to information, correction, deletion and restriction of processing, and you can object to
        processing based on legitimate interest. You can also complain to the Austrian data protection authority
        (Datenschutzbehörde).
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>
        The continents on the globe come from <a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com/">Natural Earth</a>, which is
        in the public domain.
      </p>
      <p>
        The coordinates of the cafes were looked up with OpenStreetMap: © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under
        the Open Database License. See <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">openstreetmap.org/copyright</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hard Rock Cafe is a trademark of its owner. The pins and photos are from my own collection.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .imprint {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding: 0 var(--gutter) 40px;
  }
  h1 {
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  section {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  h2 {
    font: 500 var(--text-h3) / 1.2 var(--serif);
    color: var(--brass);
  }
  p {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
  }
  .disclosure {
    padding-left: 16px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--brass);
  }
</style>
